      "html": "† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">דָּן</span></big>  <strong>nome próprio masculino. (</strong><em>juiz</em><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  filho de Jacó e Bila <a data-ref=\"Genesis 30:6\" href=\"/Genesis.30.6\">Gn 30.6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 35:25\" href=\"/Genesis.35.25\">Gn 35.25</a> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 1:4\" href=\"/Exodus.1.4\">Êx 1.4</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:47\" href=\"/Joshua.19.47\">Js 19.47</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:29\" href=\"/Judges.18.29\">Jz 18.29</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:2\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.2\">1Cr 2.2</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  a tribo de Dã, <span dir=\"rtl\">מַטֵּה דָן</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 31:6\" href=\"/Exodus.31.6\">Êx 31.6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 35:34\" href=\"/Exodus.35.34\">Êx 35.34</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 38:23\" href=\"/Exodus.38.23\">Êx 38.23</a> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 24:11\" href=\"/Leviticus.24.11\">Lv 24.11</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 1:39\" href=\"/Numbers.1.39\">Nm 1.39</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:12\" href=\"/Numbers.13.12\">Nm 13.12</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:5\" href=\"/Joshua.21.5\">Js 21.5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 21:23\" href=\"/Joshua.21.23\">Js 21.23</a> (todos P); <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי דָן</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 46:23\" href=\"/Genesis.46.23\">Gn 46.23</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 1:38\" href=\"/Numbers.1.38\">Nm 1.38</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 2:25\" href=\"/Numbers.2.25\">Nm 2.25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 7:66\" href=\"/Numbers.7.66\">Nm 7.66</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 10:25\" href=\"/Numbers.10.25\">Nm 10.25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:42\" href=\"/Numbers.26.42\">Nm 26.42</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 34:22\" href=\"/Numbers.34.22\">Nm 34.22</a> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:40\" href=\"/Joshua.19.40\">Js 19.40</a>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:47\" href=\"/Joshua.19.47\">Js 19.47</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:48\" href=\"/Joshua.19.48\">Js 19.48</a> (todos P) <a data-ref=\"Judges 1:34\" href=\"/Judges.1.34\">Jz 1.34</a> <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:2\" href=\"/Judges.18.2\">Jz 18.2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:16\" href=\"/Judges.18.16\">Jz 18.16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:22\" href=\"/Judges.18.22\">Jz 18.22</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:23\" href=\"/Judges.18.23\">Jz 18.23</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:25\" href=\"/Judges.18.25\">Jz 18.25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:26\" href=\"/Judges.18.26\">Jz 18.26</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:30\" href=\"/Judges.18.30\">Jz 18.30</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מַחֲנֵה דָן</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 2:25\" href=\"/Numbers.2.25\">Nm 2.25</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 2:31\" href=\"/Numbers.2.31\">Nm 2.31</a> (P)—sobre <a data-ref=\"Judges 13:25\" href=\"/Judges.13.25\">Jz 13.25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:12\" href=\"/Judges.18.12\">Jz 18.12</a> ver <a data-ref=\"BDB, מַחֲנֶה²\" href=\"/BDB,_מַחֲנֶה²\" dir=\"rtl\">מַחֲנֶה</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">מִשְׁפְּחֹת דָּן</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 26:42\" href=\"/Numbers.26.42\">Nm 26.42</a> (P); <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּן</span> isoladamente em poesia <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:16\" href=\"/Genesis.49.16\">Gn 49.16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:17\" href=\"/Genesis.49.17\">Gn 49.17</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 33:22\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.33.22\">Dt 33.22</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:17\" href=\"/Judges.5.17\">Jz 5.17</a>, nos demais lugares <a data-ref=\"Numbers 1:12\" href=\"/Numbers.1.12\">Nm 1.12</a> (P) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 27:13\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.27.13\">Dt 27.13</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 27:22\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.27.22\">1Cr 27.22</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:13\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.13\">2Cr 2.13</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.1\">Ez 48.1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:2\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.2\">Ez 48.2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 48:32\" href=\"/Ezekiel.48.32\">Ez 48.32</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  uma cidade na fronteira setentrional de Israel, junto a uma das nascentes do Jordão, originalmente <span dir=\"rtl\">לַיִשׁ</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:29\" href=\"/Judges.18.29\">Jz 18.29</a> (cf. v. <a data-ref=\"Judges 18:7\" href=\"/Judges.18.7\">Jz 18.7</a>); = <span dir=\"rtl\">לָשֶׁם</span> <a data-ref=\"Joshua 19:47\" href=\"/Joshua.19.47\">Js 19.47</a>; capturada por uma colônia de danitas; denominada Dã e tornada lugar sagrado com ritos de culto que perduraram até o exílio (<a data-ref=\"Judges 18:30\" href=\"/Judges.18.30\">Jz 18.30</a>); =<em>Tell el Kâdî</em>, Rob<sup>BR iii. 351, 358</sup> Bd<sup>Pal 265</sup>. A este lugar se faz frequentemente referência: <a data-ref=\"Genesis 14:14\" href=\"/Genesis.14.14\">Gn 14.14</a> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 34:1\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.34.1\">Dt 34.1</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 12:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.12.29\">1Rs 12.29</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 12:30\" href=\"/I_Kings.12.30\">1Rs 12.30</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 15:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.15.20\">1Rs 15.20</a> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 10:29\" href=\"/II_Kings.10.29\">2Rs 10.29</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 16:4\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.16.4\">2Cr 16.4</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:15\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.15\">Jr 4.15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 8:16\" href=\"/Jeremiah.8.16\">Jr 8.16</a> <a data-ref=\"Amos 8:14\" href=\"/Amos.8.14\">Am 8.14</a>: leia-se também <span dir=\"rtl\">וּבְדָן</span> em lugar de <span dir=\"rtl\">וְכֵן</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:18\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.18\">2Sm 20.18</a> 𝔊 Ew We cf. Dr; e ver a expressão <span dir=\"rtl\">מִדָּן וְעַד־בְּאֵר שֶׁבַע</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 20:1\" href=\"/Judges.20.1\">Jz 20.1</a> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 3:20\" href=\"/I_Samuel.3.20\">1Sm 3.20</a> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 3:10\" href=\"/II_Samuel.3.10\">2Sm 3.10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:11\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.11\">2Sm 17.11</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:2\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.2\">2Sm 24.2</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:15\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.15\">2Sm 24.15</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 5:5\" href=\"/I_Kings.5.5\">1Rs 5.5</a>; apresentada pelo cronista como <span dir=\"rtl\">מִבְּאֵר שֶׁכַע וְעַד־דָּן</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 21:2\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.21.2\">1Cr 21.2</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 30:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.30.5\">2Cr 30.5</a>. (<a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 27:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.27.19\">Ez 27.19</a> ver <span dir=\"rtl\">ודן</span>.)<br><em>Nota.</em> —<span dir=\"rtl\">דָּ֫נָה יַעַן</span> ou <span dir=\"rtl\">דַּנָֿה</span> (Baer) <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 24:6\" href=\"/II_Samuel.24.6\">2Sm 24.6</a>. Não se conhece tal lugar; o texto é geralmente considerado corrompido e, sendo 𝔊 incerto, é alterado de várias maneiras: (1) <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּ֫נָה יַעַר</span> <em>a Dã no bosque</em>, Thes seguindo 𝔙 <em>silvestria</em>. (2) <span dir=\"rtl\">(וַיָּסֹבּוּ) דָּ֫נָה וְעִיּוֹן</span> <em>a Dã e Ijom</em> Klo (cf. <a data-ref=\"I Kings 15:20\" href=\"/I_Kings.15.20\">1Rs 15.20</a>). (3) <span dir=\"rtl\">(סָֽבֲבוּ) דָּן וּמִדָּן</span> We Dr cf. 𝔊.",
